SOAPBOX: IC-7300, Heil Pro-Micro Headset, Vectronics VC300DLP Manual Tuner for 40
SOAPBOX: MTRS, Hy-Gain TH-5 Tri-Bander at 72 feet, and a 102' long G5RV Inverted Vee
SOAPBOX: at 70' feet. I discovered the contest on Saturday morning-Hi-Hi! but still
SOAPBOX: had fun, This was a 100% "Search and Pounce" effort. Working Morocco on 40
SOAPBOX: Meters using a G5RV and 90 watts was a real hoot! NOTE: I sent "59-03", because
SOAPBOX: "ZERO THREE" WAS THE CORRECT CQ ZONE from my location here in Morgan County,
SOAPBOX: Utah. I wonder how many Ops let their software "tell them" that I was operating
SOAPBOX: from Wyoming in CQ Zone 04? The "Worst Audio Award" goes to Italy and Brazil.
SOAPBOX: Thanks to my Dad for letting me use his Ham Shack. A five element beam at 72
SOAPBOX: feet is a wonderful thing for a contester who has relied on tree supported wire
SOAPBOX: antennas since 1989. 73, de "November Seven Many Zebras Walking".
